ve the complete meaning and caveats. Do not apply an exception to third-party reporting or community posts.\n\nFor authoritative document statements choose a complete useful fact. Preserve an exact excerpt in citations even when form=paraphrase; explicitly distinguish the restatement from the source wording. Include the scope and last-resort conditions for isolation guidance. Distinguish an agency recommendation from a legal mandate. Use the current NIST Revision 4 as durable guidance (July 2025), not an October 2026 launch. News quoting a company is not a first-party record; multiple reports copying that notice are one origin. Multi-agency joint guidance is also one origin. Select only relevant supporting sources from the topic group, not every grouped link. Defer unsupported counts even when a narrower attributed notice is usable.\n"
